The Nautilus application development team has been working on a project repository /opt/blog.git. This repo is cloned at /usr/src/kodekloudrepos on storage server in Stratos DC. 
They recently shared the following requirements with DevOps team:
Create a new branch devops in /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/blog repo from master and copy the /tmp/index.html file (present on storage server itself) into the repo. 
Further, add/commit this file in the new branch and merge back that branch into master branch. Finally, push the changes to the origin for both of the branches.

SOLUTION
Steps on Storage Server (ststor01)
SSH into the Storage server and switch to root:

bash
ssh natasha@ststor01
sudo su -
Go to the cloned blog repository:

bash
cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/blog
Make sure you are on master and create the devops branch from it:

bash
git checkout master
git checkout -b devops master
Copy /tmp/index.html into the repository:

bash
cp /tmp/index.html .
Add and commit the file on the devops branch:

bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Add index.html"
If Git complains about missing user identity, set it first:

bash
git config user.email "devops@example.com"
git config user.name "DevOps"
Then retry the commit.

Switch back to master and merge devops into it:

bash
git checkout master
git merge devops
Push both branches to origin:

bash
git push origin devops
git push origin master
Verify:

bash
git branch -a
git log --oneline --graph --decorate -5
This creates devops from master, commits index.html on devops, merges it into master, and pushes both branches to the origin remote.
